Do NOT create fake success messages. Do NOT expose API keys or SMTP credentials. Keep all secrets server-side in environment variables... If a required email provider credential/configuration is missing, clearly identify exactly what is required instead of creating a fake implementation.\"\n- **Progress**: \n  - Installed `nodemailer` in backend.\n  - Created `server/services/emailService.js` supporting standard SMTP, Gmail app passwords, Resend, and Ethereal test account fallback with full HTML templates.\n  - Added `email_notifications` tracking table in SQLite to prevent duplicate spam per day/threshold.\n  - Created `server/services/emailScheduler.js` and hooked `triggerUserEmailCheck` into mutation routes (`bills.js`, `pantry.js`, `budget.js`, `expenses.js`).\n  - Created `.env` and `.env.example` with clear instructions for Gmail and SMTP configuration.\n  - Created test email endpoint `/api/notifications/test-email` and `/api/notifications/email-logs`. Verified sending test email via Ethereal fallback when credentials are not yet entered in `.env`.\n\n### 3. Fix UI So Data Updates Without Manual Refresh (`STATUS: IMPLEMENTATION`)\n- **User Intent**: User performs action (add/delete bill, add/delete expense, change pantry quantity, add/remove pantry item, update budget) -> database changes -> UI must immediately reflect changes without manual browser refresh. Do not force full-page reloads.\n- **Progress**:\n  - Root cause 1: Express API lacked cache-control headers, causing browsers to serve cached 304/disk responses for `/api/*` endpoints. Added `Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate` in `server/index.js` and `cache: 'no-store'` in `client/src/context/AuthContext.jsx`.\n  - Root cause 2: Cross-component synchronization. Built `client/src/context/DataSyncContext.jsx` and wrapped `main.jsx` with `DataSyncProvider`.\n  - Hooked `notifyDataChanged` into:\n    - `AddBillModal.jsx`\n    - `AddExpenseModal.jsx`\n    - `AddPantryModal.jsx`\n    - `MarketPurchaseModal.jsx`\n    - `SetBudgetModal.jsx`\n  - Subscribed to `subscribeToChanges` and added optimistic updates in:\n    - `App.jsx`\n    - `Dashboard.jsx`\n    - `BillsRent.jsx` (optimistic mark as paid, optimistic delete)\n    - `Expenses.jsx` (optimistic delete)\n  - Still need to finish: hook `Pantry.jsx` (optimistic quantity adjustment & delete), `Budget.jsx`, and `ExpenseSummary.jsx`.\n\n### 4. Add PKR as Default Currency (`STATUS: IMPLEMENTATION`)\n- **User Intent**: Add Pakistani Rupee (PKR) as supported and default currency across bills, expenses, budgets, pantry, totals, summaries, and pie charts. Keep all existing currencies (`$`, `€`, `£`, `₹`, `C$`, `A$`, `¥`, `CHF`).\n- **Progress**:\n  - Created `client/src/utils/currency.js` with `CURRENCIES` having PKR (`₨ / Rs.`) at index 0 as default, `getCurrencySymbol()`, and `formatAmount()`.\n  - Updated `server/db/database.js` users table schema to `DEFAULT 'PKR'`.\n  - Updated `server/routes/auth.js` to default `currency = 'PKR'` in register and profile update.\n  - Updated `server/services/reminderEngine.js` and `aiService.js` to default to `PKR` / `Rs.`.\n  - Updated `Welcome.jsx`, `AddBillModal.jsx`, `AddExpenseModal.jsx`, `AddPantryModal.jsx`, `MarketPurchaseModal.jsx`, `SetBudgetModal.jsx`, `Dashboard.jsx`, `BillsRent.jsx`, and `Expenses.jsx` to use `getCurrencySymbol(user?.currency)`.\n  - Remaining: update `Pantry.jsx`, `Budget.jsx`, `ExpenseSummary.jsx`, `AIFeatures.jsx`, and `Navbar.jsx` to use `getCurrencySymbol(user?.currency)`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. User Knowledge\n\n- **Key User Constraints**:\n  - *\"The application is already implemented. DO NOT rebuild, redesign, simplify, reset, or remove existing functionality.\"*\n  - *\"First inspect the existing codebase and understand the current architecture before making any changes.\"*\n  - *\"PathError [TypeError]: Missing parameter name at index 1: * originalPath: '*'\"* (Occurred when user ran `node server/index.js`).\n  - *\"Emails must actually be delivered. Do NOT simulate email delivery. Do NOT create fake success messages. Do NOT expose API keys or SMTP credentials. Keep all secrets server-side in environment variables.\"*\n  - *\"If a required email provider credential/configuration is missing, clearly identify exactly what is required instead of creating a fake implementation.\"*\n  - *\"User action → Database/backend operation succeeds → Application state/data updates → UI immediately reflects the change → No manual browser refresh required. Do NOT solve this by forcing a full-page reload after every action.\"*\n  - *\"Add Pakistani Rupee (PKR) as a supported currency. Make PKR the DEFAULT currency. New users should have PKR selected by default... Keep all currently supported currencies.\"*\n- **Existing User in Database**:\n  - `id: 2, name: 'Huma', email: 'humaakhan65@gmail.com'`. Her email notifications failed because `.env` was missing SMTP credentials.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Work Accomplished\n\n1. **Server Startup Error Fixed & Tested**:\n   - Diagnosed error in Express 5 where `app.options('*', cors(corsOptions))` threw `TypeError: Missing parameter name at index 1: *`.\n   - Removed the offending line in `server/index.js`. `app.use(cors(corsOptions))` already handles all preflight options requests.\n   - Tested startup via node: server started on `http://0.0.0.0:5000` with 0 errors and HTTP 200 health check.\n\n2. **Real Email Service & Scheduler Built**:\n   - `nodemailer` installed.\n   - `server/services/emailService.js` implemented with HTML templates for bill reminders (15d, 10d, 7d, 4d, 3d, 1d, hours-left, overdue), pantry low stock, and budget warnings.\n   - `server/db/database.js` updated with `email_notifications` table with unique constraint `(user_id, reminder_key)`.\n   - `server/services/emailScheduler.js` implemented with `startEmailScheduler()` (periodic check) and `triggerUserEmailCheck(userId)` (on-demand mutation check).\n   - Added `triggerUserEmailCheck` to `bills.js`, `pantry.js`, `expenses.js`, and `budget.js`.\n   - Added test email endpoint `POST /api/notifications/test-email` and `GET /api/notifications/email-logs` in `server/routes/notifications.js`.\n   - Created `.env` and `.env.example` documenting Gmail App Password and custom SMTP configuration. Tested delivery via Ethereal fallback when credentials are unset.\n\n3. **Data Synchronization (No-Refresh UI Updates)**:\n   - Added anti-caching headers on all `/api/*` endpoints in `server/index.js` (`Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate`).\n   - Added `cache: 'no-store'` and `Cache-Control` header to `authFetch` in `client/src/context/AuthContext.jsx`.\n   - Created `client/src/context/DataSyncContext.jsx` with `notifyDataChanged` and `subscribeToChanges`.\n   - Integrated `DataSyncProvider` into `client/src/main.jsx`.\n   - Updated `AddBillModal`, `AddExpenseModal`, `AddPantryModal`, `MarketPurchaseModal`, `SetBudgetModal` to call `notifyDataChanged()`.\n   - Subscribed `App.jsx`, `Dashboard.jsx`, `BillsRent.jsx`, and `Expenses.jsx` to `subscribeToChanges`.\n   - Added optimistic UI updates for `BillsRent.jsx` (paying and deleting bills) and `Expenses.jsx` (deleting expenses).\n\n4. **PKR Default Currency Setup**:\n   - Created `client/src/utils/currency.js` containing `CURRENCIES` (PKR at index 0), `DEFAULT_CURRENCY = 'PKR'`, and `getCurrencySymbol()`.\n   - Set `currency TEXT DEFAULT 'PKR'` in `server/db/database.js`.\n   - Set `currency = 'PKR'` default in `server/routes/auth.js` and `client/src/context/AuthContext.jsx`.\n   - Updated `server/services/reminderEngine.js` and `server/services/aiService.js` to default to `Rs.` for PKR.\n   - Updated `Welcome.jsx`, `AddBillModal.jsx`, `AddExpenseModal.jsx`, `AddPantryModal.jsx`, `MarketPurchaseModal.jsx`, `SetBudgetModal.jsx`, `Dashboard.jsx`, `BillsRent.jsx`, and `Expenses.jsx` to use `getCurrencySymbol(user?.currency)`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n\n- **Express 5 & Path-to-RegExp**:\n  - Express 5 uses `path-to-regexp` v8.\n  - Wildcard routes like `app.options('*', ...)` or `app.get('*', ...)` throw `PathError [TypeError]: Missing parameter name at index 1: *`.\n  - Preflight CORS is already handled by `app.use(cors(corsOptions))`. For 404/catch-all, use middleware `app.use((req, res) => { ... })` without a path string.\n- **Browser Caching on Fetch**:\n  - Modern browsers cache GET requests unless `Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate` is returned by the server AND `cache: 'no-store'` is passed to `fetch()`. Both have now been configured.\n- **Email Delivery Mechanism**:\n  - When SMTP credentials (`GMAIL_USER`, `GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD` or `SMTP_HOST`) are defined in `.env`, `nodemailer` connects and delivers real emails directly to external inboxes.\n  - When credentials are not yet entered in `.env`, `emailService.js` falls back to Ethereal sandbox, which logs a preview URL instead of silently failing.\n- **PKR Display**:\n  - Pakistani Rupee code is `'PKR'`, and standard symbol is `'Rs.'` or `'₨'`. `getCurrencySymbol(user?.currency)` maps `'PKR'` -> `'Rs.'` so formatting displays cleanly as `Rs. 1,500.00`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files\n- `server/index.js`\n  - Removed `app.options('*', cors(corsOptions))` (lines 28-30). Added `Cache-Control: no-store` on `/api` and started `startEmailScheduler()`.\n- `server/db/database.js`\n  - Changed default currency to `'PKR'`. Added `email_notifications` table and index (lines 96-107).\n- `server/routes/auth.js`\n  - Changed default currency in `/register` and `/profile` to `'PKR'`.\n- `server/routes/bills.js`\n  - Added `triggerUserEmailCheck(req.user.id)` to POST, PUT `/pay`, PUT `/:id`, and DELETE `/:id`.\n- `server/routes/pantry.js`\n  - Added `triggerUserEmailCheck(req.user.id)` to POST, PUT `/:id/quantity`, POST `/purchase`, and DELETE `/:id`.\n- `server/routes/expenses.js`\n  - Added `triggerUserEmailCheck(req.user.id)` to POST, PUT `/:id`, and DELETE `/:id`.\n- `server/routes/budget.js`\n  - Added `triggerUserEmailCheck(req.user.id)` to POST.\n- `server/routes/notifications.js`\n  - Added `/test-email`, `/email-logs`, and `/trigger-email-check` routes.\n- `server/services/emailService.js` (NEW)\n  - Nodemailer transporter with SMTP/Gmail/Resend/Ethereal support and HTML templates for bills, pantry, budget.\n- `server/services/emailScheduler.js` (NEW)\n  - Evaluates user reminders, dedupes with `email_notifications`, and dispatches emails.\n- `server/services/reminderEngine.js` & `server/services/aiService.js`\n  - Updated fallback currency to `PKR` / `Rs.`.\n- `.env` & `.env.example` (NEW)\n  - SMTP & Gmail configuration guide.\n- `client/src/utils/currency.js` (NEW)\n  - `CURRENCIES` array with PKR at index 0, `DEFAULT_CURRENCY = 'PKR'`, `getCurrencySymbol()`, and `formatAmount()`.\n- `client/src/context/DataSyncContext.jsx` (NEW)\n  - React context for subscribing to data mutations and broadcasting `notifyDataChanged()`.\n- `client/src/context/AuthContext.jsx`\n  - Added `cache: 'no-store'` and no-cache headers in `authFetch`. Updated `register` default currency to `'PKR'`.\n- `client/src/main.jsx`\n  - Wrapped app with `DataSyncProvider`.\n- `client/src/App.jsx`\n  - Subscribed notification badge to `subscribeToChanges`.\n- `client/src/components/Welcome.jsx`\n  - Imported `CURRENCIES` and `DEFAULT_CURRENCY`, defaulting to PKR on signup.\n- `client/src/components/Modals/AddBillModal.jsx`, `AddExpenseModal.jsx`, `AddPantryModal.jsx`, `MarketPurchaseModal.jsx`, `SetBudgetModal.jsx`\n  - Wired `useDataSync` to call `notifyDataChanged()` on success and updated amount labels to use `getCurrencySymbol(user?.currency)`.\n- `client/src/components/Dashboard.jsx`, `BillsRent.jsx`, `Expenses.jsx`\n  - Subscribed to `subscribeToChanges` for instant auto-refresh, added optimistic UI updates, and updated currency symbol to `getCurrencySymbol(user?.currency)`.\n\n### Viewed Files Landscape\n- `client/src/components/Pantry.jsx` (Lines 1-399):\n  - Needs `useDataSync